[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605202000-etzhayyim-amnesty-legal-person-debt-actor", :adr/title "ADR-2605202000: Amnesty — Legal-Person Debt Restructuring Actor (sibling to Yobel)", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605202000: Amnesty — Legal-Person Debt Restructuring Actor (sibling to Yobel)\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-05-20\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n# Context\n\n[ADR-2605201800](/90-docs/adr/2605201800-etzhayyim-yobel-debt-release-actor.edn) (yobel) restricts debt release to **natural persons** (自然人). Per its §Invariants amendment, DMN R14 short-circuits any debtor whose entityType ≠ `natural_person`. This is by design: shmita / yobel / individual jubilee / tax-amnesty-for-individuals all canonically apply to flesh-and-blood debtors.\n\n**Setting aside that scope leaves a complementary gap**: legal-person debt restructuring (sovereign + corporate) is **also** a Charter §1 mission concern (structural labor liberation is undermined when sovereign debt strangles a nation's fiscal capacity for public goods, or when corporate debt forces mass layoffs that propagate labor coercion). The historical / ongoing instruments at this layer:\n\n| Instrument | Examples | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n| HIPC (Heavily Indebted Poor Countries) Initiative | IMF/World Bank 1996, expanded 1999 | sovereign multilateral debt relief |\n| Paris Club | 1956- (Argentina, Greece, Iraq, ...) | bilateral sovereign creditor coordination |\n| Brady Bond restructuring | 1989+ (Mexico, Argentina, Brazil, ...) | commercial sovereign debt collateralization |\n| Jubilee 2000 Coalition outcomes | 2000+ | civil society pressure → multilateral debt relief |\n| Corporate Chapter 11 multi-creditor plan | US 1978+ | corporate reorganization with creditor class voting |\n| Scheme of arrangement (UK / SG / HK) | Companies Act-based | court-supervised creditor compromise |\n| 会社更生 (corporate reorganization) / 民事再生 (civil rehabilitation, corporate cases) | Japan | court-mediated corporate restructuring |\n| Sovereign debt workout (UNCTAD framework) | 2015 | post-HIPC normative framework |\n\nThese are NOT in yobel's scope by the natural-person-only invariant. They need a **sibling actor**. Without one, the religious-corp has no doctrinal runtime for institutional Charter §1 alignment at the macro debt layer.\n\n# Decision\n\nCreate **`amnesty.etzhayyim.com`** as the **legal-person** counterpart to yobel.\n\n| Property | yobel (ADR-2605201800) | amnesty (this ADR) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Name** | יובל (Hebrew, ram's horn / Jubilee) | amnesty (Greek ἀμνηστία, \"forgetfulness\") |\n| **Debtor scope** | natural persons only | **legal persons only** (sovereign / corporate / multilateral / partnership) |\n| **Doctrinal basis** | Lev 25:1-7, Lev 25:8-13, Deut 15:1-2, 永仁徳政令 1297, Boniface VIII 1300 | UNCTAD Sovereign Debt Workout 2015, HIPC framework 1996, US Bankruptcy Code §1126 (creditor class voting), Mosaic Law Lev 19:18 (community-level justice as extension of individual jubilee) |\n| **Voluntary opt-in invariant** | yes — individual creditor + debtor opt-in | yes — but with **multi-party creditor consent** (≥ 2/3 creditor class voting threshold per restructuring proposal, matching Chapter 11 §1126(c) heuristic) |\n| **Council ratification** | Lv6+ × 3 + Lv9 chair / 50% baseline | **Lv9 chair × 3 + Council Five Bootstrap consultation** / 80% quorum (higher because legal-person debt impact is macro-scale) |\n| **Substrate** | AT MST + IPFS + Base L2 | Same — but additional anchor to UN/UNCITRAL registry CID if applicable |\n| **Settlement** | USDC on Base L2 (release direction only) | USDC on Base L2 + **restructuring instruments** (haircut, rescheduling, debt-for-equity swap, debt-for-nature swap) |\n| **Cross-actor delegation** | rejects legal-person → defers to amnesty | rejects natural-person → defers to yobel |\n\n## Rite catalog (5 types)\n\n| Rite type | 名称 | 範囲 | Cross-creditor consent threshold |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `sovereign_multilateral` | HIPC / Paris Club / multilateral restructuring | 主権国家 vs 多国 / 多機関 creditor coalition | ≥ 75% creditor coalition consent |\n| `sovereign_bilateral` | 二国間 sovereign debt rescheduling / haircut | 主権国家 vs single sovereign creditor | ≥ 50% (bilateral simpler) |\n| `corporate_chapter_11` | US Chapter 11 multi-creditor plan / 会社更生 / scheme of arrangement | 法人 vs creditor classes | ≥ 2/3 of each impaired class (matching §1126(c)) |\n| `corporate_workout` | out-of-court corporate workout / forbearance | 法人 vs senior creditors | ≥ 90% (out-of-court informal — high bar to bind dissenters) |\n| `debt_for_nature_swap` | sovereign debt cancellation in exchange for conservation commitment | 主権国家 vs creditor + conservation NGO | ≥ 60% creditor + NGO accreditation |\n\n## Lexicon (8 methods — mirror yobel structure)\n\n| Method | 種別 | 用途 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `declareRestructuring` | procedure | etzhayyim 主宰者 or partner religious-corp が restructuring rite を宣言 |\n| `enrollCreditorClass` | procedure | 創設者 class が voluntary に opt-in。class voting weight + signedConsent 集合 |\n| `enrollDebtor` | procedure | 法人債務者 (sovereign / corporate / multilateral) が opt-in。**debtorEntityType=\"legal_person\" 必須**、entityType claim verification |\n| `verifyEligibility` | query | rite type 別の eligibility 判定 + cross-creditor threshold pre-check |\n| `voteOnPlan` | procedure | creditor class voting (each enrolled creditor votes for/against/abstain on the restructuring plan) |\n| `recordSettlement` | procedure | restructuring settlement 記録 (haircut % / rescheduled tenor / equity swap ratio / etc.) |\n| `listRestructurings` | query | pagination 付き rite 一覧 |\n| `getRestructuring` | query | rite 詳細 + class voting tallies + settlement details |\n\n## Cluster integration\n\n```\namnesty.etzhayyim.com (legal-person, voluntary multi-creditor)\n   ├── rejects natural-person → defers to → yobel.etzhayyim.com\n   ├── represented by → vendor:lawfirm.etzhayyim.com (court filings, sovereign legal counsel)\n   ├── falls back to → vendor:bankruptcy.etzhayyim.com (formal corporate Chapter 11 / 会社更生 / scheme of arrangement)\n   ├── eligibility   ← council SBT registry (Lv1+ for proposers, Lv9 chair × 3 for ratification)\n   ├── settlement    → ERC725 Smart Wallet + Base L2 USDC + on-chain restructuring instruments\n   ├── audit         → AT MST + IPFS append-only + UN/UNCITRAL registry mirror (optional)\n   └── publication   → app.bsky.feed.post (#sovereign-debt / #chapter11 / #debt-restructuring / #amnesty)\n```\n\n## Cross-actor symmetry with yobel\n\n```\n                    ┌─────────────────┐\n                    │  debtor DID     │\n                    │  + entityType   │\n                    └────┬────────────┘\n                         │\n              ┌──────────┴──────────┐\n              │                     │\n       natural_person        legal_person\n              │                     │\n              ▼                     ▼\n    ┌──────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────┐\n    │  yobel R14 pass  │   │ amnesty R14 pass │\n    │  (Charter §1)    │   │  (Charter §1)    │\n    └──────────────────┘   └──────────────────┘\n              │                     │\n       Council Lv6+ × 3       Council Lv9 × 3\n       Lv9 chair × 1          Five-Bootstrap consultation\n       50% quorum             80% quorum\n              │                     │\n              ▼                     ▼\n        Voluntary               Multi-class\n        opt-in                  consent voting\n        (individual)            (≥ 2/3 each impaired\n                                 class)\n```\n\nWhen a debtor enrolls in yobel and the cell determines `entityType=legal_person`, the cell returns `eligible=false, dmn_rule_fired=R14, defer_to=amnesty.etzhayyim.com`. Symmetric: amnesty's R14-equivalent rule (call it \"A14\") rejects natural-person debtors with `defer_to=yobel.etzhayyim.com`.\n\n## Phase plan (delivered incrementally — this PR is Phase 1)\n\n| Phase | Deliverable | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| **1 (this PR)** | ADR + 8 lexicons + project marker + deps.toml | **in progress** |\n| 2 | Actor scaffold — BPMN + DMN tables + 6 cell READMEs (declaration / creditor_class / debtor / vote / settlement / audit) | deferred |\n| 3 | S1 Python cells (LangGraph StateGraphs) | deferred |\n| 4 | S2 ports + pytests + orchestrator + sample HIPC fixture | deferred |\n| 5 | Solidity contracts (AmnestyRestructuringRegistry + AmnestyVoteRegistry + AmnestySettlementRegistry) — **3 contracts** because legal-person flow has voting + settlement as distinct phases | deferred |\n| 6 | Web3 ports + integration tests | deferred |\n| 7 | Council ratification proposal + Base L2 deployment runbook | deferred |\n\n# Consequences\n\n**Positive**\n- Closes the conceptual loop: yobel (natural person) + amnesty (legal person) = symmetric debt-release pair, complete coverage of Charter §1 monetary-debt dimension\n- Religious-corp doctrinal runtime extends to sovereign + corporate scale — addresses macro labor coercion via debt overhang, not just individual hardship\n- HIPC / Paris Club / Chapter 11 cases get a transparent + on-chain audit trail option (currently they rely on opaque inter-state correspondence + court papering)\n- Creditor class voting on Base L2 = first transparent on-chain implementation of §1126(c) heuristic (≥ 2/3 each impaired class) — useful precedent for civil-society oversight of corporate restructurings\n- Debt-for-nature swap rite type opens a new mechanism for sovereign environmental commitments (conservation NGO accreditation as part of consent threshold)\n\n**Negative / Risk**\n- **Higher governance bar** — Lv9 chair × 3 + Five-Bootstrap consultation is a stringent threshold. May slow down legitimate fast-moving restructurings (Greece 2012 took months — etzhayyim ratification could be similar)\n- **Political legitimacy concerns** — etzhayyim religious-corp ratifying sovereign debt restructuring sits in tension with state sovereignty norms. Mitigation: amnesty is voluntary opt-in; etzhayyim does not claim authority to compel restructuring, only to record + audit voluntary agreements + provide neutral on-chain settlement infrastructure\n- **Creditor class manipulation** — bad-faith debtor could try to manufacture creditor classes to game §1126(c). Mitigation: A13 (analog of yobel R13) enforces creditor class membership via Council SBT + cross-actor verification with vendor:lawfirm.etzhayyim.com. Bad actors flagged + Council Lv9 audit triggered\n- **Dual-substrate audit complexity** — UN/UNCITRAL registry mirror is optional but introduces inter-substrate consistency risk. Recommendation: keep mirror as informational-only at S2; promote to authoritative only after S5 production hardening\n\n**Neutral**\n- amnesty's settlement instruments are richer than yobel's (haircut / rescheduling / equity swap / nature swap vs simple release). This makes Solidity scope larger — 3 contracts instead of 2\n- deps.toml `[[projects]]` entry added\n- amnesty does NOT need cross-jurisdictional tax DMN (yobel's per-jurisdiction COD income warnings) — legal-person tax treatment is the debtor's own counsel's domain. Vendor:lawfirm.etzhayyim.com delegation is symmetric to yobel but with different per-jurisdiction tables\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\n**A. Extend yobel to handle legal persons (drop the natural-person-only invariant)** — Rejected. The just-amended natural-person-only invariant (ADR-2605201800 §Invariants) was an explicit user-driven scope clarification; reversing it is a regression. Symmetric sibling actors maintain conceptual clarity.\n\n**B. Single rite type for all legal-person debt restructuring** — Rejected. Sovereign multilateral, sovereign bilateral, corporate Chapter 11, out-of-court workout, and debt-for-nature swap have materially different consent thresholds and settlement instruments. Conflating them under one rite type would force the lowest-common-denominator threshold (probably 90% out-of-court) and exclude HIPC-style multilateral cases.\n\n**C. No separate actor — handle legal-person via vendor:bankruptcy.etzhayyim.com only** — Rejected. vendor:bankruptcy is mandatory legal procedure intelligence. Religious-corp's voluntary doctrinal stance for legal-person debt is distinct (parallel rather than fallback). Vendor handles court-mandated; amnesty handles religious-corp-witnessed multi-creditor consent.\n\n**D. Defer amnesty entirely; let users wait for yobel to mature first** — Rejected. The natural-person-only amendment to yobel made the gap explicit. Documenting it as \"out of scope\" without a sibling actor leaves a documented design hole. Better to claim the design space now even if implementation is phased.\n\n**E. Use a different Hebrew name (e.g. סליחה / mechilah)** — Rejected. \"amnesty\" (Greek ἀμνηστία, also accepted into international law vocabulary at least since the Peace of Westphalia 1648) is more recognizable for the sovereign / corporate restructuring audience. yobel is the Hebrew side for the natural-person dimension; amnesty is the international-vocabulary side for the legal-person dimension. The bilingual pairing matches the religious-corp's synthetic-doctrine posture.\n\n# References\n\n**Doctrinal / legal sources**:\n- Leviticus 19:18 — \"love thy neighbor as thyself\" reinterpreted at the institutional scale\n- UNCTAD Sovereign Debt Workout Mechanism (2015)\n- HIPC Initiative Documentation (IMF/WB 1996, 1999, 2005)\n- US 11 USC §1126(c) — Chapter 11 creditor class voting threshold\n- UK Companies Act 2006 Part 26A — restructuring plan / scheme of arrangement\n- 日本会社更生法 (Corporate Reorganization Act) + 民事再生法 §174 (corporate cases)\n- Mosaic Law Lev 19:18 — institutional reading per religious-corp Charter §1 mission\n- Paris Club Comparability of Treatment doctrine\n\n**etzhayyim ADRs (depends_on)**:\n- ADR-2605201800 — Yobel actor (sibling, natural-person scope)\n- ADR-2605192100 — Charter Mission\n- ADR-2605192200 — Charter Compliance Rider v2.0\n- ADR-2605192230 — Three-Tier Enforcement\n- ADR-2605172400 — etzhayyim/vendor 3-axis split rule\n\n**Cross-references**:\n- yobel ADR-2605201800 §Invariants → \"legal-person debt out of scope, candidate for future amnesty.etzhayyim.com actor\" — this ADR fulfills that placeholder\n- vendor:bankruptcy.etzhayyim.com CLAUDE.md §Cross-Actor: yobel rite attachment restricted to natural-person bankruptcy cases — amnesty will provide the legal-person counterpart attachment lexicon (`com.etzhayyim.apps.bankruptcy.recordAmnestyRestructuringReference`)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605202000-etzhayyim-amnesty-legal-person-debt-actor.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "etzhayyim-amnesty-legal-person-debt-actor", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-20", :adr/date "2026-05-20", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605201800-etzhayyim-yobel-debt-release-actor"], :adr/authoritative_for ["org.etzhayyim.amnesty.* lexicon family (transitional NSID: com.etzhayyim.apps.etzhayyim.amnesty.*)" "sovereign debt restructuring rite catalog (HIPC / Paris Club / Brady Bond / multilateral)" "corporate amnesty rite catalog (Chapter 11 multi-creditor amnesty / scheme of arrangement / 会社更生)" "voluntary multi-creditor / multilateral consent invariant" "3-axis split: vendor reads + etzhayyim writes via Council Lv9 multisig" "cross-actor delegation: amnesty rejects natural-person debtors → defers to yobel"]}]
